 #edb/ref 17592186415752 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415765 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415759 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415765 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415762 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415765 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415765 1077 "selection" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415765 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415762 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415765 1079 #uuid "1a4c61a4-7435-599c-afcf-0efe6b1cbdb6" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415766 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415734 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415766 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415735 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415766 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415746 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415766 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415747 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415766 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415749 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415766 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415766 1077 "selection" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415766 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415747 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415766 1079 #uuid "7adcd9af-5265-5496-ada0-3911ecad9cdc" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415767 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415736 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415767 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415739 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415767 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415754 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415767 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415757 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415767 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415761 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415767 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415767 1077 "selection" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415767 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415739 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415767 1079 #uuid "9c4c4c60-58a2-5309-91fd-f009939a8cdc" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415768 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415741 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415768 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415745 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415768 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415756 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415768 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415758 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415768 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415763 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415768 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415768 1077 "selection" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415768 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415745 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415768 1079 #uuid "b523b1e1-5cbd-5efb-b1af-a137b9b5cd25" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415769 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415738 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415769 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415740 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415769 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415743 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415769 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415755 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415769 1075 #edb/ref 17592186415760 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415769 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415769 1077 "selection" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415769 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415743 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415769 1079 #uuid "f968e9bb-1698-556c-94c3-47e9ed5d0dfa" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415770 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415766 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415770 1069 "q-77250" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415770 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415770 1071 "![](images/87/87182d625f4e669a6b2791a17f3e12c34922043b8f3deefd6b2473e8fb529886.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(2,0),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a section of the parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ from the point $A(2,0)$ to the point $B(0,4).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2,$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=x\\,i$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415770 1072 #uuid "3412530f-81b3-51bb-95a9-4599a55eb207" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415770 1074 "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the first integral, so we only need to work out the second.\n\nLet ${C}_{2}$ be the section of parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ from $A$ to $B.$ Then,\n $-{C}_{2}$ will be the same path but travelled from $B$ to $A.$ The path $-{C}_{2}$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}(t)=t\\,i+(4-{t}^{2})\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<2.$ Along this curve, we have $x=t$ and $y=4-{t}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t)) & =x\\,i=t\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4-{t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i-2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =(t\\,i)\\cdot (i-2t\\,j) \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =2-{\\int }_{0}^{2}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2-{\\int }_{0}^{2}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2-{[\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2-[\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415771 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415764 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415771 1069 "q-77148" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415771 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415771 1071 "![](images/0c/0c3b1312e7368d8fc760a274a49280b10d4571a06ee6237b28fc8a8b1b7316d3.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $DEFD,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the **clockwise** direction?" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415771 1072 #uuid "4ab286f6-317f-53cd-ac02-bf3eb20fe604" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415771 1074 "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in clockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {-{C}_{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{3}$ is the same path as ${C}_{3}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415772 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415767 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415772 1069 "q-77134" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415772 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415772 1071 "![](images/74/746a05b2345e50173ed898b741944ba435d17a44dfc075848be9d8fcd2f2ad90.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $PQRP,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the counterclockwise direction?" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415772 1072 #uuid "6da1b103-36df-5031-b2ef-46cb571416a8" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415772 1074 "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in counterclockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC={-{C}_{1}}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{1}$ is the same path as ${C}_{1}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415773 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415769 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415773 1069 "q-125425" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415773 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415773 1071 "If ${\\int }_{C}(y-z)\\,\\text{d}x+6{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z$ is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for some piecewise smooth curve $C,$ then $F(x,y,z)=$" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415773 1072 #uuid "6fc12b03-7934-57bc-b6a6-b1ef9ff5ade7" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415773 1074 "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y+R\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nIn our case, $P=y-z,Q=6{z}^{2},R=-4y.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}((y-z)\\,i+6{z}^{2}\\,j-4y\\,k)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}(y-z)\\,\\text{d}x+6{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-4y\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $F=(y-z)\\,i+6{z}^{2}\\,j-4y\\,k.$" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415774 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415768 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415774 1069 "q-77244" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415774 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415774 1071 "![](images/b4/b4ce481ac8babb7a3e5707f1ef44417b12e73abe4b4c2143c19b45332642c6d2.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment  from the point $B(0,8)$ to the point $A(-2,8),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a section of the curve $y=-{x}^{3}$ from the point $A(-2,8)$ to the point $O(0,0).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=16,$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=xy\\,i+y\\,j$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415774 1072 #uuid "8399ab15-70cf-5db8-b1d1-61088de736be" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415774 1074 "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the first integral, so we only need to work out the second.\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the section of the curve $y=-{x}^{3}$ from $A$ to $O.$ It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}(t)=t\\,i-{t}^{3}\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $-2\\le t\\le 0.$ Along this curve, we have $x=t$ and $y=-{t}^{3}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t)) & =xy\\,i+y\\,j \\\\  & =-{t}^{4}\\,i-{t}^{3}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{t}^{3})j \\\\  & =i-3{t}^{2}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =(-{t}^{4}\\,i-{t}^{3}\\,j)\\cdot (i-3{t}^{2}\\,j) \\\\  & =-{t}^{4}+3{t}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =16+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =16+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(-{t}^{4}+3{t}^{5})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =16+{[-\\frac{1}{5}{t}^{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{6}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =16+[0-(-\\frac{(-{2}^{5})}{5}+\\frac{(-2)^{6}}{2})] \\\\  & =16-\\frac{192}{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{112}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415775 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415765 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415775 1069 "q-125419" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415775 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415775 1071 "Let $F(x,y)={e}^{y}\\,i+{e}^{x}\\,j$ and let $C$ be the path defined by $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t-1⟩$ for $t\\in [0,1].$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415775 1072 #uuid "a47f5f1d-1328-52e8-8c90-bfca32946e28" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true] [17592186415775 1074 "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x+{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534246 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-126d13a7-71fa-5051-a4a2-28f29e56cf03" 17592186415734 "answer-2216ca5d-6c6a-5107-a068-323114e3fc15" 17592186415735 "answer-248f19de-9914-5bab-a8d3-9da16c44f98d" 17592186415736 "answer-3124c0f4-4c6e-55ec-9349-8032b33b382f" 17592186415737 "answer-44901697-c22c-53ba-bb65-14f1081533bb" 17592186415738 "answer-46aa7018-0782-59bf-8f3c-c481140a5532" 17592186415739 "answer-49a222b7-ced0-5334-a476-927827cacddd" 17592186415740 "answer-55fc80b9-6193-508c-b227-e04b2840c9d6" 17592186415741 "answer-57f5be3d-e9a5-5b71-9237-641c57905868" 17592186415742 "answer-6829492d-3f92-5206-8c0f-7015db0fd5bb" 17592186415743 "answer-6f4582a3-9b84-5136-bbc8-4a5b81e6b276" 17592186415744 "answer-7527daea-f713-54e2-9b27-ffd3fc3bb110" 17592186415745 "answer-7aae6b46-36e9-538a-8e22-b5381b749d2c" 17592186415746 "answer-7e44c518-6f87-55b7-bbc1-4